# TDPD Product Delivery

Read `.tdpd/core/FRAMEWORK.md`, select the relevant manifest under `.tdpd/core/layers/`, and read only its owned modules plus shared gates and roles. Use `full` only for complete lifecycle work.

Use Shape, Plan, Deliver, or Audit mode. Planning and auditing do not authorize implementation. Validate evidence, opportunity, business viability, and measurement before delivery. After UAT, validate GTM, govern launch and outcomes, and record the lifecycle decision.

Before implementation, require an approved product surface, interface contract and inventory, and project organization contract. Do not default to a CLI or engineering-only interface when the user surface is unspecified. E2E acceptance must exercise the approved surface.

Scale role reviews to risk. Do not claim TDPD completion without green executable scenarios and explicit human UAT; otherwise state **engineering complete, awaiting UAT**.
